---
description: Keep UI, commands, and domain edits on separate sides of the architecture
alwaysApply: true
---

# Architecture boundaries

UI reads session signals and changes state by dispatching a `Command` through `CommandBus`. `SessionService.apply` is the only writer of session state.

- Put document and geometry edits in pure functions under `src/app/core/`.
- Keep pointer state, snapping, and dispatch in the viewport. Keep geometry in `src/app/viewport/utils/`.
- Use `@vector-editor/*` for imports across domains. Use relative imports inside one domain.
- Do not add imports that cycle `core`, `commands`, `viewport`, and `panels`.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — a panel edits the document
document.objects.push(created);

// ✅ GOOD — the panel dispatches; the session applies the command
this.bus.dispatch({ type: 'object.delete', ids });
```
